# Security

- Never expose secrets (API keys, JWT secrets, Bachs keys, SMTP passwords, webhook secrets).
- Never log credentials or secrets.
- Never trust frontend prices. Recalculate payable amounts on the backend from database package prices.
- Enforce authorization server-side on every admin and privileged route. Do not rely on hidden UI.
- Validate all external input (body, query, params, webhooks, uploads).
- Never commit `.env` files or Bachs keys.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
console.log("login", { email, password });
booking.amountKobo = dto.amountKobo;

// ✅ GOOD
booking.amountKobo = pricingService.onlinePriceKobo(pkg.priceKobo);
```
